Source: "blit-raster.s"
                            	     1: ; raster.s split in two for blit.s. The VBL only swaps the buffer pointers (the main loop has already written the
                            	     2: ; new screen address) and starts MFP timer A. Its interrupt runs the timed palette writes of raster.s, unchanged
                            	     3: ; from .no_swap on and synchronised to the display start by the video counter, so the top border until then
                            	     4: ; belongs to the main loop.
                            	     5: ; TIMER_A_TICKS: delay at 2.4576 MHz / 50 (163 CPU cycles a tick). The display starts about 17,700 cycles after
                            	     6: ; the VBL. The interrupt has to come before that even when the VBL and the timer interrupt both wait for the
                            	     7: ; longest Blitter block in HOG mode (about 3,100 cycles each): 58 ticks are about 9,450 cycles.
                            	     8: 
                            	     9: 	ifnd TIMER_A_TICKS
                            	    10: TIMER_A_TICKS equ 58
                            	    11: 	endc
                            	    12: 
                            	    13: spectrum_vbl:
